{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01071",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.3,
      "end_seconds": 4.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Hi there, the chair's free, sit down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.25,
      "end_seconds": 10.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Mm, hello, thanks for fitting me in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.69,
      "end_seconds": 14.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "How are things, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.39,
      "end_seconds": 19.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "well, I've been having a missed period"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.25,
      "end_seconds": 23.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.88,
      "end_seconds": 27.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Thyroxine. I take it 75 micrograms, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.13,
      "end_seconds": 32.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.53,
      "end_seconds": 36.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "for one week, I'd say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.12,
      "end_seconds": 41.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Right, is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.46,
      "end_seconds": 44.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Moderate, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.87,
      "end_seconds": 52.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.1,
      "end_seconds": 74.76,
      "duration_seconds": 20.66,
      "text": "I mean, it usually comes with nausea in the mornings. The nausea in the mornings? That's been for five days. Um, with nausea in the mornings, severe, I'd say. Oh, uh, and I've been feeling tired as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.78,
      "end_seconds": 82.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any fever, severe abdominal pain, dizziness or vomiting everything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.81,
      "end_seconds": 88.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "So, no, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.78,
      "end_seconds": 93.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.04,
      "end_seconds": 96.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "nothing else aches"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.41,
      "end_seconds": 102.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.23,
      "end_seconds": 107.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "My heart's been fine, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.73,
      "end_seconds": 119.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.41,
      "end_seconds": 130.11,
      "duration_seconds": 9.7,
      "text": "Yes, wheat. I've no idea what the reaction was, only that I'm not supposed to have it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.93,
      "end_seconds": 133.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.3,
      "end_seconds": 142.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "Okay, so yes, I had a varicose vein procedure, last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.77,
      "end_seconds": 163.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "what do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.74,
      "end_seconds": 169.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.06,
      "end_seconds": 172.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.43,
      "end_seconds": 178.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.22,
      "end_seconds": 180.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.98,
      "end_seconds": 187.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.18,
      "end_seconds": 193.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.4,
      "end_seconds": 204.47,
      "duration_seconds": 9.07,
      "text": "I have an underactive thyroid, for two years. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.99,
      "end_seconds": 213.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Alright, an underactive thyroid, that matches what I have here. Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.11,
      "end_seconds": 225.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.8,
      "end_seconds": 246.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "okay: temperature is 36.5 degrees, blood pressure 123 over 79. And saturation 97 percent, pulse 70."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.05,
      "end_seconds": 251.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.52,
      "end_seconds": 255.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Okay, stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.26,
      "end_seconds": 280.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "tummy is soft, non-tender, and the uterus isn't palpable above the pelvic bone yet"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.95,
      "end_seconds": 285.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.84,
      "end_seconds": 311.58,
      "duration_seconds": 12.74,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. It's hard to say. An early pregnancy is one possibility and and a late period for another reason another, and I'd rather not commit yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.66,
      "end_seconds": 316.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Is it it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.14,
      "end_seconds": 334.6,
      "duration_seconds": 17.46,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with an early pregnancy do well once it's treated properly i think blood tests makes sense here, for antenatal screening i want an early scan done, that's for early pregnancy"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.91,
      "end_seconds": 337.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Right, understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.83,
      "end_seconds": 377.13,
      "duration_seconds": 34.3,
      "text": "I think a pregnancy test makes sense here, for missed period i'll start you on folic acid, 5 milligrams, once a day, until twelve weeks that should help with pregnancy small, frequent meals and dry crackers before getting out of bed can calm the morning nausea avoid alcohol and don't take any new tablets without checking with us first cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.89,
      "end_seconds": 383.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Do get help quickly if you have bleeding or sharp pain on one side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.46,
      "end_seconds": 389.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "um, yes, I'll bear that in mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.46,
      "end_seconds": 397.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "I'll want another look after the scan. Okay, is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.23,
      "end_seconds": 401.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}